hot-3 — Environment frame representation (plan-3).

Make the environment a flat, index-addressable structure so hot-2's addresses are
cheap to follow.

WHAT
- Represent a lexical frame as a small VECTOR of slots (not an alist of
  name->value/local-variable structs): frame = { parent, slots[n] }, indexed by the
  hot-2 slot index.  Allocate the slot vector sized by the analyzed local count.
- Keep the SPECIAL/dynamic binding stack SEPARATE (a shadowing stack of
  symbol/old-value pairs restored on unwind), so lexical access never walks dynamic
  bindings and special access never walks lexical frames.  DEFVAR/PROGV/LET-of-a-
  special push there.
- Preserve the debugger's per-frame info (the call frame records function +
  environment for backtraces — see [[bocl-defun-lexical-block]]): keep enough
  metadata on the frame for backtrace even with vector slots.
- GC: frames are ordinary heap objects (non-moving GC keeps raw slot pointers valid);
  auto-rooted via allocate().  Watch the write barrier when storing into an older
  frame (cf. gc_write_barrier usage).

ACCEPTANCE: binding/closure/special-variable suites (control, restarts, must-control)
green; measured allocation/lookup reduction vs the alist frames; no GC regressions
(run BOCL_GCMINORSTRESS-style checks where applicable, mindful of the known
minor-gc-doomed issue).

DEPENDS ON: hot-2.
